://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":13198400136,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-aiA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:complete","name":"audit:complete","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"PR fully implemented spawning issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-11-09T05:18:53Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T11:21:04Z","closed_at":"2026-11-09T05:19:37Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/7975","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7975","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7975.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/7975.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-09T05:19:37Z"},"body":"Fixes #2832. Design #3068 Phase 2 (parsed files in tools) for sync-models.\n\n## Problem\nA parseable-but-wrong-shaped `opencode.jsonc` (`\"google\": \"oops\"`, `\"models\": \"oops\"`, an array provider entry, or no `provider` key at all) crashed sync-models with raw TypeErrors naming neither the file nor the key — in `run()`'s provider derefs and in the JSONC tree editor's `members` walks — blocking sync for every provider until a human guessed the bad key.\n\n## Changes (bin/sync-models.mjs)\n- **`validateConfigShape(config, configPath)`** runs immediately after `parseJsonc` in `run()`, in the same clean-exit path as a parse error: root, `provider`, each provider entry, and each `models` container must be plain objects, otherwise one named error — `invalid config shape in <path>: provider.google: expected object, got string`. Whole-job refusal with a diagnostic, per the #3068 Phase 2 leaning recorded for #2832.\n- **Missing `provider` key = nothing to sync**, not a crash: the two remaining `config.provider` derefs (antigravity block, openai sync) now use optional chaining.\n- **Tree editor guards:** `setJsoncPath` / `removeJsoncPath` refuse a non-object intermediate node with an error naming the full key path and the offending prefix, instead of dereferencing `members` on a scalar/array node.\n\n## Tests (bin/sync-models.test.mjs)\nNew #2832 tests pin: scalar provider entry, array provider entry, scalar `models`, wrong-shaped `provider` container and root, missing `provider` key (no throw), well-formed config (no throw), tree-editor refusal for scalar/array intermediates, and the well-formed set control. Laptop run: `node --test bin/sync-models.test.mjs` — 35 pass, 0 fail (all pre-existing tests stay green). Oracle: the named-error messages above; before this change the same shapes threw `Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'find')` / `Cannot create property … on string 'oops'`.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796793536&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7975&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7975&signature=49a4c9fb1ca885b435e1e2590c804e0c0a7043edc437b6b3d332c1f5a8ad9302\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7975?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7975/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/7975/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197","id":6442076589,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABPyqpBg","number":11197,"title":"Fix #7983 item 1: sync-models validates the language-server catalog shape","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":12834279439,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAAC_PuQDw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/status/in-progress","name":"status/in-progress","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"Queue worker lifecycle state","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":12834737120,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAAC_QKL4A","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/work/assigned","name":"work/assigned","color":"FEF2C0","default":false,"description":"Queue worker lifecycle state","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":13198401025,"node_id":"LA_kwDOJWP4788AAAADEq-eAQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/labels/audit:gap-filed","name":"audit:gap-filed","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":"Gap/next-step filed as new issue","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-11-17T10:02:55Z","updated_at":"2026-11-24T02:17:00Z","closed_at":"2026-11-17T21:37:19Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/11197","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/11197.patch","merged_at":"2026-11-17T21:37:19Z"},"body":"Closes item 1 of #7983 (parse-boundary shape checks, #3068 contract).\n\n## Change\n- `bin/sync-models.mjs`: the language-server `GetAvailableModels` response was read as `(await res.json()).response?.models || {}`, so shape drift read as zero models. It now goes through `parseLiveCatalogBody`, which requires a plain object body, a plain-object `response`, and a plain-object `response.models`. Any other shape throws a named `LiveCatalogShapeError` that is rethrown past the per-port probe loop instead of being swallowed. Malformed JSON (a syntax failure) keeps the existing per-port skip.\n- `bin/sync-models.test.mjs`: probe matrix (null, array, scalar, `{}`, wrong-typed `response` and `response.models`) plus a well-formed case.\n\n## Note on the site\nThe issue text places the site at the models.dev read (`:127`). The quoted expression `.response?.models || {}` is the language-server read at `:137` in this tree. This PR fixes that expression. The models.dev read at `:87` (`fetchModelsDev`, returns the parsed body unchecked) is not changed here; it is left for a follow-up item if the chain needs it.\n\n## Tests\n- `node --test bin/sync-models.test.mjs` — 55 pass, 0 fail.\n- `node --check bin/sync-models.mjs` — OK.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1797501777&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=11197&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F11197&signature=ea680921540a9bd8897dd3e938c29471816ccc4d3b315fb35cd20d87509be644\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/11197?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/11197/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"