zren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/2489","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2489","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2489.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2489.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-30T04:16:16Z"},"body":"Completes the core rewrite for #1858, following the verified map in `pkgs/mcpx/docs/opencode-plugin-v2.md` §6 (groundwork PR #2457, merged). Related: #730 (the fleet's deployed `.opencode/plugin/` copy — a different artifact; this core's shape is what gets ported there under #730, not in this PR).\n\n**The v2 tree** (`pkgs/mcpx/plugin/opencode/v2/`, beside the untouched v1 files):\n- `index.ts` — `export default { id: \"mcpx\", setup }`; setup wires storage warm-read, context hook, session-env, timing, and tool registration last (registration can never fail setup)\n- `options.ts` — v1 `Options` + resolution for every setting the core consumes, property reads of declared names only (settings guard)\n- `session-env.ts` — `PUT /api/session/:id/environment` once per session with the **full** env (route replaces; doc §3), quiet degrade with no `serverUrl`\n- `context.ts` — idempotent system-prompt paragraph via `session.hook(\"context\")`\n- `remember.ts` — remembered daemon on `ctx.storage`, until-gone via health-check drop; no state file\n- `timing.ts` — `execute.after` records for both statuses of the union (failures recorded, not just successes)\n- `tools.ts` — `tool.transform` registration under the `mcpx` namespace: `discover` / `exec` / `observe` plus `daemon_status` / `daemon_select` / `daemon_forget`, gated exactly as v1 (tools opt-in; daemon tools when asked, when the full set is on, or when boot discovery is ambiguous). Verified against the pin: `editor.namespace({ name, description })`, plain JSON Schema inputs, and `effectiveName` flattening means the model still sees `mcpx_exec` etc. §7's namespace question is resolved in the doc.\n- `daemon.ts` — re-export of the shared harness-free daemon core (socket-first per #53/#44, reused not rewritten)\n\n**Honest v2 differences** (recorded in tools.ts): the v2 ToolContext has no `ctx.ask`, so `daemon_select` applies the choice directly instead of confirming; there is no TUI channel in the server context slice, so ambiguity rides the tool-result annotation line rather than toasts.\n\n**NOT in this PR — the SET-REMAINDER on #1858**, to be enqueued when this core lands: sampling answers via `ctx.generate.text`, `mcp.transform` filtered per-session registration, `permission.hook(\"evaluate\")`, and the promise-based TUI `select()` daemon picker. Server-side `_meta['ai.opencode/sessionID']` attribution is #1932's tracked work, not this PR.\n\n**Tests:** `bun test plugin/opencode/v2/` — 15 pass (context/storage/session-env + the new tools.test.ts: registration names, gating, executor fallbacks, storage-backed select scopes); full plugin suite 50 tests, 0 fail, on the laptop worktree. Go settings guards (`TestThePluginReadsNoUndeclaredSetting`, script-env) run in CI over the new tree.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added support for the OpenCode v2 plugin, with configurable daemon discovery and CLI fallback.\n  * Added tools for discovering, running, and observing commands, plus managing daemon selection and status.\n  * Added optional session instructions, environment syncing, and tool execution timing.\n  * Added daemon choices that can be remembered for a session or longer, with health checks to discard unavailable daemons.\n  * Tools and optional features remain disabled by default unless enabled in configuration.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2489/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2489/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2250","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2250/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2250/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2250/events","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2250","id":6098124395,"node_id":"PR_kwDOJWP4788AAAABLf-woQ","number":2250,"title":"feat(openclaw): opencode-route provider proxy — OpenCode server front for OpenClaw (#2229)","user":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-10-29T10:54:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-30T00:59:51Z","closed_at":"2026-10-30T00:59:49Z","assignee":{"login":"dezren39","id":11225574,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjI1NTc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11225574?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39","html_url":"https://github.com/dezren39","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dezren39/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/pulls/2250","html_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2250","diff_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2250.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/developing-today/code/pull/2250.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-30T00:59:49Z"},"body":"Method 3 of code#2229: an OpenAI-compatible front so OpenClaw can run jobs carried by the OpenCode workhorse route.\n\n## What\n- **bin/opencode-route-proxy.mjs** (new): chat-completions facade on fixed port **18750** (next free in the #437 block), mirroring the commandcode proxy pattern. Each request creates one session on the laptop OpenCode server via its v2 API (`POST /api/session` with `model:{providerID:\"opencode-route\", id:<pool>}`), prompts it, waits for settle, and returns the assistant text as a chat completion. Streaming supported via message polling. OpenAI tool_calls are not round-tripped — the OpenCode build agent executes with its own tools server-side (documented in the file header).\n- **bin/opencode-route-proxy-start.sh** + **bin/opencode-route-proxy.test.mjs** (new; tests pass 2/2).\n- **home/common/default.nix**: `opencodeRouteProxyPort = 18750`, proxy-supervisor entry, manual-fallback systemd unit (no Install.WantedBy — the supervisor owns the process, per the 2026-10-26 commandcode lesson).\n- **home/openclaw/default.nix**: `models.providers.opencode-route` (workhorse, speed, specialist, summit, scout), gateway After/Wants on the proxy unit, laptop-operations port list updated.\n\n## Live proof (2026-10-29, from this worktree)\n- `POST /v1/chat/completions {model:\"opencode-route/workhorse\"}` → `ROUTE-PROXY-OK`.\n- `openclaw agent --local --model opencode-route/workhorse` → replied **OC-ROUTE-OK**; run meta: provider `opencode-route`, model `workhorse`, fallbackUsed=false.\n- Verified in the OpenCode v2 tables: session **ses_e5e78b6f4f4ffeVyPSZquFZkwV** (\"opencode-route-proxy: workhorse\"), assistant carried by providerID `opencode-go`, model `deepseek-v4.1-flash`, variant `high` — the workhorse pool door.\n\nDeploys permanently at the next switch (supervisor takes over port 18750 from the checkout).\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/2250?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795863248&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=2250&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F2250&signature=fc0e6176865f20b483f070ab6d5123f26d43876bb1009ff7aa1262dcf086704d\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added a local OpenAI-compatible endpoint for health checks, model listings, and chat completions.\n  * Added five selectable OpenCode models: Workhorse, Speed, Specialist, Summit, and Scout.\n  * Chat completions support both streaming and non-streaming responses, with usage information included for streaming.\n  * The service restarts automatically if it stops, and completion requests have a configurable timeout.\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Invalid or empty requests and unavailable upstream services now return clear error responses.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2250/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/developing-today/code/issues/2250/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"score":1.0}],"search_type":"lexical"}